cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Kastner IT Research Archive"
abstract: >
  A structured archive of research studies, articles, memoirs,
  expert reports, and related artifacts (1972-2026) centered on the work
  of Peter S. Kastner at Aberdeen Group, Arthur D. Little,
  Philip Hankins Inc. (PHI) Computer Services/Wang, Digital Equipment
  Corporation, Stratus Computer, Prime Computer and Obian Group, plus
  contributions from other Aberdeen analysts. Each study is packaged as a
  self-contained Frictionless Data Package with structured CSV tables for
  studies, entities, technologies, observations, and codes; a
  datapackage.json descriptor; a schema_org.json discovery layer; and a
  human-readable README. The archive is fully audited (Layer A per-study
  referential integrity, Layer B CSV write validation, Layer C cross-study
  cache integrity) with zero failures. Current corpus shape and prescience
  surfaces are published in the generated ARCHIVE_STATS.md. The archive
  carries full-corpus long-horizon prescience scoring plus fixed 3-year and
  5-year short-horizon reads (with window-elapsed validation on the
  short-horizon scorer) and PC Deals per-SKU price journeys. Version 2.1.1
  is a documentation and repository-hygiene release with no data, schema,
  or scoring change from v2.1.
